# Tool input validation

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| Issue | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft |

The registry owns input validation so every executor receives input accepted by its registered JSON Schema.

## Contract

- "'`execute` rejects missing required properties, wrong types and invalid enum members before invoking an executor, returns a corrective `ToolResponse` naming the property path and failed constraint without values in results or logs, passes valid input including unknown properties unchanged exactly once without defaults or coercion, and preserves the `Unknown tool: <name>` exception for unregistered names.
- Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten subsequent executions reuse the compiled schema without reading it again.
- Function-valued definitions resolve at execution time and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name.

## Integration and release

The returned rejection uses the existing tool-result conversation path, allowing the model to correct a call within the existing tool-round bound. Executor exceptions are outside the input-validation contract.

Implementation also updates README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md, adds the validator as a runtime dependency, points the one-line execute comment here, and publishes a MINOR migration note in CHANGELOG.md and the PR description explaining that executors no longer receive malformed input.
